#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 89
#: rc.cpp:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface type"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 91
#: rc.cpp:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the type of the interface to monitor. KNetLoad 3 supports two types "
"of interfaces: local and SNMP remote.\n"
"This setting determines which settings will be applied in the corresponding "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 94
#: rc.cpp:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local Interface"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 96
#: rc.cpp:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A local interface is an interface present in the machine where KNetLoad is "
"running.\n"
"Load data about this interface will be requested from the operating system, "
"depending on how it is supported in KNetLoad."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 99
#: rc.cpp:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote (SNMP) Interface"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 101
#: rc.cpp:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remote interfaces are accessed using the net-snmp library to connect to the "
"SNMP server.\n"
"Example of uses of remote SNMP interfaces are routers, printers, miscellaneous "
"servers, switches..."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 107
#: rc.cpp:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface name"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 109
#: rc.cpp:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the interface, such as eth0, ppp0 or lo.\n"
"This is dependant on the operating system you are running."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 112
#: rc.cpp:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "Active"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 114
#: rc.cpp:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the network load monitor.\n"
"This option is provided when the CPU is doing expensive work, or when the "
"remote interface is not available (for example, if the network is down), to "
"avoid useless SNMP requests."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 118
#: rc.cpp:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "SNMP Server"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 119
#: rc.cpp:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Server's IP or hostname to monitor the interface of."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 122
#: rc.cpp:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "Community string"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 124
#: rc.cpp:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Community's name to use to read the server's interface statistics.\n"
"This is something like a password, but in many cases is simply the 'public' "
"literal (without quotes)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 128
#: rc.cpp:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "SNMP Version"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 132
#: rc.cpp:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the version used for the SNMP requests. Currently supported versions "
"are SNMPv1 and SNMPv2.\n"
"They both use a blend authentication with a simple &quot;community&quot; which "
"is the password for reading from (or writing to) the values.\n"
"\n"
"Most SoHo routers supports SNMPv1."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 144
#: rc.cpp:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input scale"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 146
#: rc.cpp:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The maximum value for the input graph.\n"
"If this value is 0, it will take the &quot;Output scale&quot; value."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 150
#: rc.cpp:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scale output"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 153
#: rc.cpp:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The maximum value for the output graph.\n"
"If this value is 0 and the interface is a remote one, the value will be "
"retrieved from the SNMP server's statistics.\n"
"If this value is 0 and the interface is a local one, the graphs are disabled."
msgstr ""

